# Context-Appropriate Example Values

**RULE: Infer example values from prop/parameter names and types. Use guiding, context-appropriate examples instead of generic placeholders.**

## Principle

Example values should help developers understand the expected format. Use the name and type to choose an appropriate value—avoid `"example"` when something more specific would guide better.

## Patterns to Apply

| Context | Prefer | Avoid |
|---------|--------|-------|
| Reference numbers | `"REF-12345"` | `"example"` |
| Callbacks with value params | `(value) => console.log('X', value)` | `() => console.log('X')` |
| SKU/UID/ID | `"PRODUCT-SKU-123"`, `"abc-123"` | `"example"` |
| Email | `"user@example.com"` | `"example"` |
| URLs | `"https://example.com"` | `"example"` |

## When Adding New Patterns

1. Check if the prop/parameter name suggests a specific format (e.g. `reference` → reference number).
2. If formats vary by system, use a generic-but-recognizable example (e.g. `"REF-12345"` for reference numbers).
3. Add the pattern to `inferExampleValue()` in `scripts/lib/markdown/example-generator.js`.

## Reference

See `scripts/GENERATOR-RULES.md` for the full list of patterns and implementation details.
